","924540a1-ed2d-516d-b799-2b1f807e1bee","8f5874c8-041f-56f5-aa12-c87373e166ea","336322aa-12f7-5320-84f3-3708916ba5fb","dd85e1c9-e232-5422-93e0-be678b885d13","61029b7c-4aab-5312-89d4-063d4ec4fa8c","b0e0c3e4-1dda-5f05-bcfd-bc354123d691"]},{"name":"slot_door","origin":[0.0,0.0,-57.0],"color":0,"uuid":"8ebe7a0e-57f5-514c-a46f-862674f12815","export":true,"mirror_uv":false,"isOpen":false,"locked":false,"visibility":true,"autouv":0,"rotation":[0,0,0],"children":[]},{"name":"fx_smoke","origin":[-50.0,218.0,4.0],"color":0,"uuid":"f8171c70-8315-5b77-981d-2a3b1cdcecc4","export":true,"mirror_uv":false,"isOpen":false,"locked":false,"visibility":true,"autouv":0,"rotation":[0,0,0],"children":[]},{"name":"fx_smoke_2","origin":[50.0,218.0,4.0],"color":0,"uuid":"a80408eb-cfd5-506b-8d8b-b539f77ec4b7","export":true,"mirror_uv":false,"isOpen":false,"locked":false,"visibility":true,"autouv":0,"rotation":[0,0,0],"children":[]},{"name":"slot_dropoff","origin":[50.0,0.0,-62.0],"color":0,"uuid":"7727c728-bbdc-5870-8e20-aa3b2a6e66b9","export":true,"mirror_uv":false,"isOpen":false,"locked":false,"visibility":true,"autouv":0,"rotation":[0,0,0],"children":[]}]}],"textures":[{"path":"main_base_l5.png","name":"main_base_l5.png","folder":"","namespace":"","id":"0","width":256,"height":1024,"uv_width":256,"uv_height":1024,"particle":false,"use_as_default":true,"layers_enabled":false,"sync_to_project":"","render_mode":"default","render_sides":"auto","frame_time":1,"frame_order_type":"loop","frame_order":"","frame_interpolate":false,"visible":true,"internal":true,"saved":true,"uuid":"dfd376ea-ea47-5605-9d2e-ef4fa2f1294f","relative_path":"main_base_l5.png","source":"data:image/png;base64,"}],"animations":[],"description":"# main_base_l5\n\nMain base level 5, Marble Hall (the first marble level): marble ground floor, porch and window sills, timber-framed upper storey, slate roof, stone chimneys.\n\n- Footprint: 14 x 14 columns (224 x 224 units, 6.30 x 6.30 m), centred on the origin, front (door side) faces -Z.\n- Finished bounds: x -112..112, y 0..217, z -112..112 units.\n- Texture: 256 x 1024, 1 px per unit, square pixels, nearest filtering. Every visible face has its own texture region painted with its material at world position (seams line up across faces); identical faces share a region; construction and ruined pieces map into the region of the face they were cut from. No cube is cut to fit the texture.\n- Cubes: finished 207, construction_0 31, construction_33 81, construction_66 106, ruined 46 (8 rotated: roof slabs and a few leaning props).\n\n## Hit box\n\n- hall: 176 x 200 x 120 (w x h x d) centred at x 0, z 4\n\n## State group sets (children of `root`; show exactly one)\n\n- `finished`: the finished building (visible by default).\n- `construction_0`, `construction_33`, `construction_66`: build progress at 0 %, 33 % and 66 % (staked outline and scaffold, then walls rising inside scaffold, then full frame with roof rafters).\n- `ruined`: collapsed shell, broken walls, rubble, fallen roof (use with `_damaged.png`, or `_abandoned.png` for F7 abandoned buildings).\n- `main_base_l5_damaged.png`: damaged texture (scorch, holes, cracks) for the same UVs; works on every group set.\n- `main_base_l5_abandoned.png`: abandoned look (damage plus moss, faded cloth, cold fires) = `abandoned_main_base_l5` together with the `ruined` set or the finished set.\n\n## Attachment and effect points (empty groups)\n\n- `slot_door` at (0, 0, -57)\n- `fx_smoke` at (-50, 218, 4)\n- `fx_smoke_2` at (50, 218, 4)\n- `slot_dropoff` at (50, 0, -62)\n"}